                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237594761",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198121334503",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 3199,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 3199,
                            "last_played": 1791848541
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love this game, but it's so unforgiving to casual players. It is laughably easy to accidentally put a coin in the wrong slot and lose hours of real time because of it.\r\n\r\nThis in itself isn't the main issue: while it can be annoying to lose some progress from a silly mistake, my real problem is that you can lose gems permanently when you die. It's disappointing that I would have to play a perfect save in order to unlock everything. This is a heavy punishment that you can't turn off, and I don't play video games enough to have the time or energy to start a new save from scratch for some cool/useful extras, especially when silly mistakes are inevitable. I wish that my deaths could just be \"setbacks\" rather than barring me from experiencing the full game by permanently losing my gems.\r\n\r\nI've played this game on and off for about three years now (a save in the base Two Crowns and another in the DLC Call of Olympus), for the beautiful graphics and addicting gameplay, but it's always a small mistake exploding into a catastrophic loss that makes me stop playing for a few months. If I knew that I could get my stuff back without needing to start a new save file, I would be a lot more motivated to keep playing right away.\r\n\r\nThat being said, I really do recommend this game. It's fun to immerse yourself in the world and to be the next heir rebuilding after a long reign. And the music is great!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1791852085,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1791852085,
